      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "While presets could be useful they won’t solve too much when it comes to managing performance. \nI personally hate the performance in large instances such as the events because you can’t just show the avatar on an individual, you have to start bypassing the whole safety settings to see someone and over multiple events that starts to add up. Not being able to show individual safety and performance settings or have a per instance temporary option can make these settings useless if we have to constantly permanently show everything on everyone. \nThis can be applied to public instances I don’t wish to permanently show everything on users just to see their avatar when I’m running max safety and performance settings for multiple reasons.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
